title: Right coalition collapses
subtitle: The right-wing coalition has collapsed...
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: traditionalist_ideology == "Radical" and year == 1928 and month >= 11 and in_right_coalition == 1
on-arrival: was_in_right_coalition = 1
max-visits: 1

= Mallin's exit from the coalition

One of Mallin's first acts as leader of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> is to terminate the coalition with the propertied parties as expected. There is no other possible paths to a majority that excludes us, leaving us to determine whether Askew continues governing or not.

We can either vote to bring down the government and hold new elections, or "tolerate" a government led by the remaining propertied parties. Alternatively, we could enter a reorganized Askew cabinet.

- @join_bruning
- @vonc_yes
- @vonc_no  
- @no_matter

@join_bruning
title: We will join the Askew coalition.
subtitle: The chancellorship will remain with Askew.
view-if: grand_coalition >= 50 or neo_weimar_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: marcher_in_government = 1; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; in_grand_coalition = 1; in_right_coalition = 0; chancellor = "Askew"; chancellor_party = "Unionist"; foreign_minister_party = "Gold"; foreign_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; interior_minister_party = ddp_name; justice_minister_party = ddp_name; justice_minister_party  = "LVP" if lvp_formed; labor_minister_party = "Unionist"; army_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = "Gold"; economic_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; finance_minister_party = "Unionist"; agriculture_minister_party = "Unionist"; leverage = 25 if leverage >= 25; burgher_traditionalist -= 2; guild_traditionalist -= 2; landed_traditionalist -= 2; left_dissent += 8; ddp_left += 1; lvp_left += 0.5; heartland_negotiations_trigger = 1 if (in_center_right_coalition_heartland or in_right_coalition_heartland)

[? if in_center_right_coalition_heartland or in_right_coalition_heartland: The Heartland coalition isn't able to survive either, pressure from Mallin and his supporters forces the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> to exit from the <span style="color: #000000;">propertied</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> coalition there as well. ?]

Edmund Askew welcomes us into his new cabinet. Now, we have our pick of ministries.

- @election_1928.ministries: Now, we must select our ministries.

@vonc_yes
title: Support the vote of no confidence, voting against the government.
subtitle: The government will collapse, and there will be new elections.
view-if: neo_weimar_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; in_right_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; pro_republic -= 2; gold_relation -= 4; unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; ddp_cohesion -= 0.5; ddp_right += 0.5
call: set_next_election_time
go-to: new_prussia_election if (in_center_right_coalition_heartland or in_right_coalition_heartland)

The right-wing coalition has fallen. New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@vonc_no
title: Support the rump [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]-led government, voting in favor of the government.
subtitle: We would essentially provide "toleration" to a propertied government.
view-if: neo_weimar_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: marcher_toleration = 1; in_right_coalition = 0; in_center_right_coalition = 0; left_dissent += 8
go-to: new_prussia_election if (in_center_right_coalition_heartland or in_right_coalition_heartland)

By supporting the government, we have essentially entered into a "toleration" arrangement with the [+ chancellor +] government. We do not have a voice in the government, but we are responsible for its continued stability. The left of our party opposes this plan, and would rather that we hold new elections.

@no_matter
title: It does not matter what we do.
subtitle: The anti-government parties have over 50% of the vote, no matter our choices.
view-if: neo_weimar_coalition < 50
call: set_next_election_time
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; in_right_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; pro_republic -= 5
go-to: new_prussia_election if (in_center_right_coalition_heartland or in_right_coalition_heartland)

The right-wing coalition has fallen. New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@new_prussia_election
on-arrival: heartland_coalition_trigger = 1

The Heartland coalition isn't able to survive either, pressure from the national conservatives within the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> forces them to exit from the <span style="color: #000000;">propertied</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> coalition there as well.

- @prussian_coalition_formation: Negotiate a new Heartland coalition.
